 "result": "Method: `Config.load_env_prefixed` in `src/tessel/config.py:126`. Conversion function: `json.loads`, the default for the `loads` parameter (`config.py:127`).\n\nNothing in `src/` calls it, so the app must call `app.config.load_env_prefixed()` itself.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Prefix.** `prefix` defaults to `\"TESSEL\"`. Line 152 turns it into `\"TESSEL_\"`.\n\n2. **Scan.** Line 154 loops over `sorted(os.environ)`, so keys load in alphabetical order. Names without the prefix are skipped.\n\n3. **Strip.** Line 159 uses `key.removeprefix(prefix)`:\n   - `TESSEL_SECRET_KEY` becomes `SECRET_KEY`.\n   - `TESSEL_DB__HOST` becomes `DB__HOST`.\n\n4. **Convert.** Line 162 calls `loads(value)`, which is `json.loads` by default.\n   - `\"5432\"` becomes `int` 5432.\n   - `\"true\"` becomes `True`.\n   - `'[\"a\",\"b\"]'` becomes a list.\n   - `'{\"x\":1}'` becomes a dict.\n   - On any exception, the value stays a plain string (lines 163–165). So `s3cret` stays `\"s3cret\"`.\n   - You can pass a different `loads` callable.\n\n5. **Flat key.** If `\"__\"` is not in the key, line 169 sets `self[key] = value`, so `SECRET_KEY` is set directly.\n\n6. **Nested key.** Line 174 splits on `\"__\"` into `*parts, tail`. For `DB__HOST`, `parts` is `[\"DB\"]` and `tail` is `\"HOST\"`.\n   - Lines 176–181 walk `parts` from `self`. A missing intermediate key is created as `{}`.\n   - Line 183 sets `current[tail] = value`, which gives `config[\"DB\"][\"HOST\"]`.\n\n7. **Return.** The method always returns `True`.\n\n**Caveats**\n\n- If an intermediate key already holds a non-dict, such as a string, the walk at line 181 breaks. The `part not in current` check passes, then `current[tail] = value` fails.\n- Sorted order means `TESSEL_DB` loads before `TESSEL_DB__HOST`. A JSON dict set in `TESSEL_DB` gets `HOST` added to it. The reverse order would not work.",
